{"nodes": [{"id": "context_ram_measurement", "label": "Mesure RAM NUCLEO-F439ZI \u2014 contigu\u00eft\u00e9 .bss et pic r\u00e9el", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/context/ram_measurement.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_ram_measurement_bss_contiguity", "label": "Contigu\u00eft\u00e9 de la zone [_sbss, _ebss]", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/context/ram_measurement.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Une section de sortie du linker est par d\u00e9finition un bloc d'adresses contigu\u00ebs : _ebss - _sbss = taille .bss exacte, sans trou ni intrus ; v\u00e9rifi\u00e9 par 4 sources concordantes (size, objdump, symboles, runtime) = 105 036 B."}, {"id": "context_ram_measurement_ram_peak", "label": "ram_peak = .data + .bss + pic de pile", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/context/ram_measurement.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": ".bss exclut la pile o\u00f9 vivent les gros buffers locaux (hv[HDC_DIM] = 4 Ko) ; le claim Gap 2 doit s'appuyer sur ram_peak, pas seulement .bss. Mesur\u00e9 : 460 + 106 152 + 4 712 \u2248 111 324 B (42,5 % de 256 Ko)."}, {"id": "context_ram_measurement_stack_painting", "label": "Stack painting / high-water mark (canary position-d\u00e9pendant)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/context/ram_measurement.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Chaque mot de la zone pile libre re\u00e7oit sa propre adresse au boot ; le canary position-d\u00e9pendant \u00e9limine le faux n\u00e9gatif d'un buffer rempli d'une constante r\u00e9p\u00e9t\u00e9e. Restitution via OpenOCD sans toucher au protocole UART (r\u00e8gle anti-DEBUG_PRINTF)."}, {"id": "context_ram_measurement_static_stack_bound", "label": "Borne statique de pile (-fstack-usage)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/context/ram_measurement.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Le pic mesur\u00e9 d\u00e9pend de la charge stream\u00e9e ; on le confronte \u00e0 une borne statique issue des .su GCC (0 impact code g\u00e9n\u00e9r\u00e9). Pas de r\u00e9cursion, dispatch par switch \u2192 cha\u00eene pire-cas auditable : 4 768 B \u2265 pic mesur\u00e9 4 712 B, les deux m\u00e9thodes se corroborent."}, {"id": "context_ram_measurement_shared_frame_thesis", "label": "Th\u00e8se \u00ab trame partag\u00e9e \u00bb pipeline_run()", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/context/ram_measurement.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Le compilateur r\u00e9serve une seule trame pour pipeline_run() = max de ses branches (dont hv[HDC_DIM] 4 Ko) : le pic de pile (~4,3\u20134,7 Ko) est une propri\u00e9t\u00e9 du firmware entier, non isolable par mod\u00e8le, peu sensible aux dims (k=5\u219221 : .bss explose 105\u2192185 Ko mais pile +16\u2026+56 B)."}], "edges": [{"source": "context_ram_measurement", "target": "src_profiling", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/context/ram_measurement.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "context_ram_measurement", "target": "startup_startup_stm32f439xx", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/context/ram_measurement.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "context_ram_measurement", "target": "linker_stm32f439zitx_flash", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/context/ram_measurement.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "context_ram_me